    {
        "content": "<p>8 messages were moved here from <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"579630\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/579630-Project-announcements/topic/WASM64.20.2B.20lean.20-.20QED64/with/618652075\">#Project announcements &gt; WASM64 + lean - QED64</a> by <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110087\">Kim Morrison</span>.</p>",
        "id": 633514922,
        "sender_full_name": "Notification Bot",
        "timestamp": 1792555071
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1028523\">@Fawad</span> was kind enough to roll a prototype variant of <a href=\"https://impermeable.github.io/aquarium/\">the Waterproof Aquarium</a> combined with our (Verbose) Lean configuration based on his work and I must say it's very promising. The memory size requirement is probably the main constraint, and it can be a bit unstable here and there, but after the intial load it was quite responsive for me. </p>\n<p>I'm looking forward to where this can lead: it's really nice for educational deployments to be able to run client-side in the browser. Even if you need to fall back to a native installation for some fraction of students, it reduces the support burden a lot, and running a live-Lean-like server with enough capacity to support hundreds of students is unfeasible for us.</p>",
        "id": 633548076,
        "sender_full_name": "Pim Otte",
        "timestamp": 1792567804
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh thank You Pim! Very nice of you. I will try to keep improving it. Areas I will be focusing on, memory usage(which should address crashes) and stack overflow. I think speed is decent at the moment. Feel free to open issues on the repo and I will try to address them. Once Safari gives support for WASM64 then it should be supported on all browsers</p>",
        "id": 633650205,
        "sender_full_name": "Fawad",
        "timestamp": 1792590194
    }
]